# Git push

The remote is `origin`, `https://github.com/alexxvives/releva.git`.

When a task is finished and the validation gate has passed, commit that task and push it to `origin` on the current branch.

- One commit per finished task. Do not commit or push after every edit.
- Stage only the files that belong to that task. Leave unrelated working-tree changes unstaged.
- Never commit `.env` or any secret. Never print a connection string, key, or password.
- Never force-push. Never skip hooks.
- The shell is Windows PowerShell. Commit with `git commit -m "message"`. Do not use a bash heredoc.
- The message is one or two sentences on why the change exists, matching `git log`.
